---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const pageTitle = 'Privacy Policy — Typeframe';
const pageDescription =
  'What Typeframe does and does not collect. No accounts, no analytics, no ad scripts, and no upload endpoint. Drafts stay in your browser.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  url="https://typeframe.pages.dev/privacy-policy/"
>
  <main class="page">
    <div class="prose-wrap">
      <header class="prose-header">
        <p class="page-kicker">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="prose-title">Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="page-lead">
          Typeframe is a static site with a local editor. This page describes the
          small amount of data involved in serving it, and the much larger amount
          that never leaves your browser.
        </p>
        <p class="prose-meta">Effective November 2026</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <section>
          <h2>The short version</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>No accounts and no sign-in.</li>
            <li>No advertising, analytics, or tracking scripts.</li>
            <li>No server-side storage of your text, settings, or photos.</li>
            <li>Drafts are saved in your browser and, when you choose, in the URL.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
          <p>
            Typeframe renders with the browser's Canvas API. The text you type,
            the typography and surface settings you choose, and any background
            image you upload are held in the page's memory and processed locally.
            There is no upload endpoint, and the site has no application server
            or database that could receive them.
          </p>
          <p>
            The current composition is saved to your browser's
            <code>localStorage</code> under the key <code>typeframe-draft</code>,
            so a reload does not discard your work. The same state is encoded into
            the page URL. If you copy a share link, anyone who opens that link can
            decode the text and settings it contains. Treat a shared link the way
            you would treat a shared document.
          </p>
          <p>
            Clearing site data for <code>typeframe.pages.dev</code> removes the
            local draft. A private browsing window discards it when the window
            closes.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>What the site receives</h2>
          <p>
            Typeframe is served as a static site by Cloudflare Pages. Like any
            hosting provider, Cloudflare may process request metadata such as your
            IP address, browser user agent, requested URL, and timestamps in order
            to deliver the site and protect it from abuse. Typeframe does not have
            access to your compositions through this process.
          </p>
          <p>
            Typeframe itself sets no cookies. There are no first-party or
            third-party advertising cookies, no analytics identifiers, and no
            session recording.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Third parties</h2>
          <p>
            The site loads no advertising networks, analytics services, social
            embeds, or third-party font CDNs. Typefaces are self-hosted as WOFF2
            files, so setting type does not make a request to Google or any other
            font service.
          </p>
          <p>
            Pages may link to external sites such as X or GitHub. Those links only
            send data when you follow them, and the destination's own privacy
            policy applies from that point.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Your choices</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Clear site data in your browser to remove the local draft.</li>
            <li>Use a private window to work without leaving a stored draft.</li>
            <li>Disable JavaScript if you only want to read the written pages; the editor itself requires it.</li>
            <li>Email <a href="mailto:support@typeframe.pages.dev">support@typeframe.pages.dev</a> with any privacy question.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Because Typeframe has no accounts and keeps no server-side profile,
            there is no personal profile to export or delete. If you believe the
            hosting layer holds data about you, write to the address above and we
            will help identify the right route.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            If the way the site handles data changes, this page will be updated
            and the effective date will move. A change that affects what leaves
            your browser would be called out on this page rather than buried in a
            revision history.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this policy can be sent to
            <a href="mailto:support@typeframe.pages.dev">support@typeframe.pages.dev</a>.
            The <a href="/terms/">terms of service</a> cover use of the studio
            itself.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
